# Gate fixtures: data that happens to be Markdown/JSON, whose exact bytes are the
# evidence that `check_gate_fixtures.py` asserts exit codes over. `pnpm format`
# is MANDATORY before every commit and runs --write across this glob, so it is
# the rewriting tool most likely to touch these files and was the only one with
# no disposition. Two of them carry deliberate control bytes; prettier's markdown
# parser treats U+2028 as a line terminator and would silently normalise it.
#
# Note 9 of the 14 markdown fixtures were already ignored BY ACCIDENT -- the
# unanchored CONTEXT.md / DELIVERY_PLAN.md patterns above match at any depth --
# and anchoring those (a reasonable future tidy-up) would have removed that
# coverage with nothing to notice. This line is the deliberate version.
#
# LOAD-BEARING ON THE HARNESS RUNNING, like the ruff/black/test-integrity
# exclusions: if the "gates can fail" step goes away, this goes with it.
apps/api/tests/gates/
